WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:06.180
In 1475, in southern Italy, the
first dated Hebrew book was printed.

2
00:00:06.230 --> 00:00:10.040
It was not the Torah itself,
but one man's notes on it.

3
00:00:10.090 --> 00:00:13.920
His name was Rashi, of
Troyes, in northern France.

4
00:00:13.970 --> 00:00:18.500
Today his notes sit in the inner
column of printed Talmud pages.

5
00:00:18.550 --> 00:00:23.820
Why does almost every printed Torah and
Talmud carry the notes of this one man?

6
00:00:23.870 --> 00:00:27.620
In this mission, you'll read Rashi
on the first verse of Genesis,

7
00:00:27.670 --> 00:00:30.110
and meet the pupils who questioned him.

8
00:00:30.160 --> 00:00:34.060
Then you'll weigh up whether he is the
most important Jewish commentator of the

9
00:00:34.110 --> 00:00:35.480
Middle Ages.

10
00:00:35.530 --> 00:00:40.520
Your mission: find out why one man's
notes surround the Torah and the Talmud.
